# No end-of-line conversion, anywhere. Git's default on Windows (`core.autocrlf=true`) rewrites
# checked-out files to CRLF, and this repo cannot afford that in either direction:
#
#   - `scripts/setup.mjs` checked out with CRLF fails to parse inside the Workers test pool, so
#     `npm test` broke on a fresh Windows clone (12 tests, the whole self-hosting setup suite)
#     while passing on the machine where the file had been written with LF.
#   - The HTML fixtures are byte-for-byte captures of real MyAnimeList pages, `\r` included — one
#     of them exists precisely to pin a bug where MAL emits a stray `\r` inside an href. Letting
#     Git normalise those bytes would silently rewrite the evidence the parser tests rest on.
#
# So: store what is committed, check out what is stored.
* -text
